+# LOSSY-VERIFICATION PILOT PATCH (not upstream vLLM).
+#
+# Speculative Cascades [Tok], LOSSLESS-TAIL variant (spec-casc-tok-lt). This
+# repo's own experiment on top of Narasimhan et al. 2025's token-level
+# deferral rule (their Eq. 15: r(x, v) = 1 iff p(v) < (1-alpha) * max_w p(w)),
+# used as a hard per-token switch instead of the blended pi_Token target the
+# paper (and this repo's spec-casc-tok patch) builds from it:
+#
+#   x in A     iff  p(x) >= (1-alpha) * max_w p(w)      (verifier's trusted top set)
+#   accept     iff  x in A (always), OR x not in A and p(x)/q(x) >= u (strict)
+#
+# Why this exists: plain spec-casc-tok is pi_rej(v) = q(v) + eta*p(v) inside
+# A and eta*p(v) outside, eta = 1 - q(A). Inside A both rules accept with
+# probability 1; OUTSIDE A spec-casc-tok accepts with probability
+# min(1, eta*p(x)/q(x)) <= min(1, p(x)/q(x)) -- STRICTER than lossless, since
+# eta <= 1. The campaign found spec-casc-tok to be the one relaxation that
+# never inflates completion length, but also the one with the narrowest
+# reachable mean-accepted-length band. This variant keeps the "free pass
+# only inside the verifier's own head" part and replaces the out-of-set
+# penalty with the ordinary lossless test, so it accepts weakly more than
+# both strict and spec-casc-tok at every alpha. If its completion length
+# stays flat while its acceptance rises, the length inflation elsewhere is
+# attributable to committing tokens OUTSIDE the verifier's head, not to
+# relaxation per se; if it inflates, the eta penalty was load-bearing.
+#
+# Not a normalised relaxed target: the induced per-token target is q on A
+# and p off A, which does not sum to 1 in general. That is fine for the
+# accept test (it is a per-token rule, exactly like the paper's Eq. 15
+# switch) and residual/recovery sampling stays on stock p, unmodified --
+# same structural shape as this repo's spec-casc-opt/r-fuzzy patches, which
+# also only touch the accept test.
+#
+# alpha domain is (-inf, 1]. alpha -> -inf makes (1-alpha)*max p exceed every
+# p(x), so A is empty, every position defers, and the kernel runs exactly
+# the strict test: that is the strict point, NOT alpha = 0 (at alpha = 0, A
+# is the verifier's own argmax and a drafted argmax token is accepted
+# unconditionally instead of with probability min(1, p/q)). Same trap as
+# spec-casc-tok; same -inf missing-file default, for the same reason.
+#
+# Mechanically this patch is spec-casc-opt's patch with a different
+# per-token boolean mask: the Triton kernel hunk is byte-identical
+# (defer=True -> strict test, defer=False -> accept). The mask needs the
+# drafted token's own verifier probability and the verifier's top-1, both
+# cheap gathers/reductions done once in plain PyTorch before launch.
+#
+# The alpha value comes from a file, not the environment: vLLM spawns
+# EngineCore with a sanitised environment, so env vars never reach the
+# sampler (see the other patches' identical note). The path is uid-scoped
+# under /tmp so a clone in any directory agrees with the server script.
+_SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-spec-casc-tok-lt-alpha-{os.getuid()}"
+try:
+    with open(_SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_FILE) as _f:
+        _SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA = float(_f.read().strip())
+    _SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_SOURCE = _SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_FILE
+except (OSError, ValueError):
+    _SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA = float("-inf")  # always defer -> exactly strict spec-dec
+    _SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_SOURCE = f"default, no readable {_SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_FILE}"
+print(
+    f"[SPEC-CASC-TOK-LT PATCH] pid={os.getpid()} alpha={_SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA} "
+    f"({_SPEC_CASC_TOK_LT_ALPHA_SOURCE})",
+    file=sys.stderr,
+    flush=True,
+)
